ses the server-side `resources/read` invocation count so the client\n./examples/caching/server.ts:63:    server.registerTool('read-count', { description: 'Number of resources/read calls that reached this server' }, async () => ({\n./examples/caching/client.ts:58:// `readResource`: the resource handler counts how many times it ran, and\n./examples/caching/client.ts:60:const read = (await client.readResource({ uri: 'config://app' })) as Cacheable & Awaited<ReturnType<typeof client.readResource>>;\n./examples/caching/client.ts:67:await client.readResource({ uri: 'config://app' });\n./examples/caching/client.ts:71:await client.readResource({ uri: 'config://app' }, { cacheMode: 'refresh' });\n./examples/caching/client.ts:75:await client.readResource({ uri: 'config://app' });\n./docs/clients/roots.md:7:Pass paths through tool arguments, resource URIs, or host configuration instead. **Roots** are deprecated as of protocol version 2026-07-28 (SEP-2577) and stay functional on 2025-era connections for at least twelve months — see the [deprecated features registry](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/draft/deprecated).\n./docs/clients/roots.md:82:- Roots are deprecated (SEP-2577): pass paths through tool arguments, resource URIs, or configuration instead.\n./docs/clients/calling.md:80:`listResources` names what the server exposes; `readResource` fetches one URI.\n./docs/clients/calling.md:82:```ts source=\"../../examples/guides/clients/calling.examples.ts#readResource_basic\"\n./docs/clients/calling.md:86:const { contents } = await client.readResource({ uri: 'orders://recent' });\n./docs/clients/calling.md:101:For parameterized URIs, `listResourceTemplates()` returns the server's URI templates — expand one and pass the resulting URI to `readResource`. To react when a resource changes instead of re-reading it on a timer, see [Subscriptions](./subscriptions.md).\n./docs/clients/calling.md:176:- `readResource({ uri })` and `getPrompt({ name, arguments })` follow the same list-then-fetch shape as tools.\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:322:            'A request handler that throws McpError(code, message, data) produces a JSON-RPC error whose error.data equals the thrown data; the client-side rejection is an McpError with .data deep-equal to the original object.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:519:            'A tool whose advertised outputSchema declares a $schema dialect URI the built-in validator does not recognise is refused gracefully on the client: callTool throws InvalidParams with a clear \"unsupported dialect … 2020-12 only\" message instead of having the underlying engine fail opaquely.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:524:            'One bad outputSchema in a tools/list response (a schema the validator engine refuses to compile — e.g. an unresolvable external $ref) does not poison the listing: tools/list resolves with every tool present, callTool on the bad tool throws InvalidParams, and callTool on the other tools succeeds.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:547:            'A tool whose advertised outputSchema declares no $schema is validated by the client with the 2020-12 engine (the default): a 2020-12-only keyword (prefixItems) in the schema is enforced, so structuredContent violating it causes callTool to throw InvalidParams.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:726:        behavior: 'resources/read returns binary contents base64-encoded in blob.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:730:        behavior: 'Variables extracted from a templated resource URI reach the resource function as typed arguments.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:734:        behavior: 'resources/read returns text contents carrying uri, mimeType, and the text.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:739:            'resources/read for an unknown URI returns JSON-RPC error -32602 (Invalid Params) with data.uri echoing the requested URI; clients also recognise -32002 from older peers. Servers do not return an empty contents array for a non-existent resource.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:794:            'The deprecated McpServer.resource() overloads (fixed-URI and ResourceTemplate, with and without the optional metadata arg) register a resource that surfaces in resources/list and reads via resources/read identically to registerResource().',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:900:            'completion/complete with a ref naming an unknown prompt or non-matching resource URI returns JSON-RPC error -32602 (Invalid params).'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:963:                note: 'Protocol wraps schema-parse failures as -32603 (InternalError), not -32602 (InvalidParams) as required by JSON-RPC 2.0.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2504:            'A resource_link returned by a tool call can be followed with resources/read on the linked URI to retrieve the referenced contents.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2505:        note: 'Stateless hosting creates a fresh server per request and has no standalone GET stream, so there is no server→client channel to deliver/observe these. The createMcpHandler entry arms are included: the body is plain client→server request/response (a tools/call, then a resources/read against the same statically-registered factory), so the per-request entry serves it on both eras.'\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2531:                note: \"McpServer's tools/call handler catches the output-validation ProtocolError (-32602) and returns it as an isError result instead of a JSON-RPC error; the nonconforming structuredContent is still withheld from the caller.\"\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2546:                note: \"McpServer's tools/call handler catches the input-validation ProtocolError (-32602) and returns it as an isError result, so callTool() resolves instead of rejecting; the handler is still not invoked.\"\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2561:                note: \"McpServer's tools/call handler catches the input-validation ProtocolError (-32602) and returns it as an isError result, so callTool() resolves instead of rejecting; the handler is still not invoked.\"\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2658:            'Typed tools/list, resources/read and resources/list round trips negotiated on 2026-07-28 over a createMcpHandler endpoint succeed, and the wire results carry resultType \"complete\" plus the required ttlMs/cacheScope fields, with the configured-hint precedence observable on the wire: the per-resource cacheHint wins over the per-operation cacheHints entry (resources/read), a per-operation hint wins over the defaults (tools/list), and a result with no configured author is filled with the ttlMs 0 / cacheScope private defaults (resources/list).',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2666:            'A factory with every cache-hint author configured (per-operation cacheHints and a per-resource cacheHint), served to a plain 2025 client through the legacy stateless slot of a createMcpHandler endpoint, answers tools/list and resources/read with no resultType, ttlMs, cacheScope or cacheHint vocabulary anywhere in the response bytes.',\n./test/e2e/requirements.ts:2878:            'A JSON-RPC error response surfaces on the requesting side as a ProtocolError carrying the wire error code (e.g. -32602) and message, distinguishable from SDK-side SdkErrors.'\n./docs/clients/caching.md:17:await client.readResource({ uri: 'config://app' }, { cacheMode: 'bypass' }); // no cache read or write\n./docs/clients/caching.md:24:resources/read requests that reached the server: 1\n./docs/clients/caching.md:39:            'resources/read': { ttlMs: 5_000, cacheScope: 'private' }\n./docs/clients/caching.md:45:`registerResource` also takes a per-resource `cacheHint`; it wins, field by field, over the `resources/read` entry here for that resource's read results. Mark a result `cacheScope: 'public'` only when it is identical for every caller — anything derived from the caller's authorization context stays `'private'`, the default.\n./docs/clients/caching.md:53:`cacheMode` on `listTools()`, `listPrompts()`, `listResources()`, `listResourceTemplates()`, and `readResource()` — the cacheable verbs — takes one of three values. `'use'`, the default, serves a still-fresh entry and otherwise fetches and stores. `'refresh'` always fetches and stores the fresh result.\n./docs/clients/caching.md:59:`responseCacheStore` swaps the backing store; the default is a fresh `InMemoryResponseCacheStore` per client, holding at most 512 `resources/read` entries.\n./docs/clients/caching.md:100:- `listTools()`, `listPrompts()`, `listResources()`, `listResourceTemplates()`, and `readResource()` serve a still-fresh result without a round trip; `cacheMode` overrides per call.\n./examples/caching/README.md:10:The client calls `listTools()` and `readResource()` twice each; the second of each pair is served from the response cache. The server exposes a `request-count` tool (how many `tools/list` requests reached it) and a `read-count` tool (how many times the resource handler ran), so the example asserts each counter is unchanged after the cache-served call and increments after `cacheMode: 'refresh'`.\n./examples/caching/README.md:14:Per-call control on the cacheable verbs (`listTools()` / `listPrompts()` / `listResources()` / `listResourceTemplates()` / `readResource()`):\n./examples/caching/README.md:17:await client.readResource({ uri: 'config://app' }); // 'use' (default): serve from cache if fresh\n./examples/caching/README.md:18:await client.readResource({ uri: 'config://app' }, { cacheMode: 'refresh' }); // always fetch, then re-store\n./examples/caching/README.md:19:await client.readResource({ uri: 'config://app' }, { cacheMode: 'bypass' }); // fetch; do not read or write the cache\n./examples/stickynotes/client.ts:52:const read = await client.readResource({ uri: firstNote.uri });\n./packages/client/src/client/client.ts:70:    ProtocolError,\n./packages/client/src/client/client.ts:71:    ProtocolErrorCode,\n./packages/client/src/client/client.ts:213:     * `resources/read` with an `input_required` result instead of sending a\n./packag