{ uri: 'res://x' });\n./packages/client/test/client/responseCache.test.ts:1241:        expect(store.get({ method: 'resources/read', params: 'res://x', partition: part('alice') })).toBeUndefined();\n./packages/client/test/client/responseCache.test.ts:1245:        const next = client.readResource({ uri: 'res://x' });\n./packages/client/test/client/responseCache.test.ts:1250:        expect(store.get({ method: 'resources/read', params: 'res://x', partition: part('alice') })).toBeDefined();\n./packages/client/test/client/mcpParamMirroring.test.ts:473:        await tx.send(modernRequest('resources/read', { uri: 'file:///レポート.md' }));\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/enums.ts:5:export enum ProtocolErrorCode {\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/enums.ts:10:    InvalidParams = -32_602,\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/enums.ts:17:     * Receive-tolerated only: the SDK never EMITS `-32002` — `resources/read`\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/enums.ts:18:     * misses answer `-32602` (Invalid Params) on every protocol revision per\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/types.ts:553: * tool parameters, resource URIs, or configuration.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/types.ts:559: * tool parameters, resource URIs, or configuration.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/types.ts:565: * tool parameters, resource URIs, or configuration.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/types.ts:571: * tool parameters, resource URIs, or configuration.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/types.ts:580: * `prompts/get`, `resources/read`) returns an input-required result carrying\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/types.ts:620: * (`tools/call`, `prompts/get`, `resources/read`) returns to request more\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/types.ts:689:    'resources/read': ReadResourceResult;\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/types.ts:708: * `prompts/get`, `resources/read`) additionally accept an\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/types.ts:716:    [M in keyof ResultTypeMap]: M extends 'tools/call' | 'prompts/get' | 'resources/read'\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/types.ts:769:export interface InvalidParamsError extends JSONRPCErrorObject {\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:45:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - `resources/read` for an unknown URI now answers with JSON-RPC error code `-32602`\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:46:  (Invalid Params) on every protocol revision, with `error.data.uri` echoing the\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:56:    `ProtocolErrorCode.ResourceNotFound` (`-32002`) remains importable as receive-tolerated\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:59:    class carries `data.uri`, and `ProtocolError.fromError` reconstructs it from a `-32602`\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:62:    stays a generic `ProtocolError`.\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:70:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Results of the cacheable 2026-07-28 operations (`tools/list`, `prompts/list`, `resources/list`, `resources/templates/list`, `resources/read`, `server/discover`) now always carry the revision's required `ttlMs`/`cacheScope` fields when served on that revision, defaulting to `ttlMs: 0` / `cacheScope: 'private'`. Servers can configure the emitted values with the new `ServerOptions.cacheHints` option (per operation) and the new `cacheHint` member of the `registerResource` config (per resource); resolution is per field, most specific author first: cache fields returned by a handler win over the per-resource hint, which wins over the per-operation hint, and configured hints are validated at construction/registration time (`RangeError` on invalid values). Responses on 2025-era connections are unchanged and never carry these fields. Note for untyped callers: `registerResource` now interprets a `cacheHint` key in its config object — it is validated and kept out of the resource's list metadata, where it was previously passed through as ordinary metadata.\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:87:- [#2381](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2381) [`f0bf785`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/f0bf785239af67f0cfce24575fec9c1193deaff1) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Serve `input_required` handlers on 2025-era connections: the legacy shim (on by default) converts each embedded request of an `input_required` return into a real server→client request (`elicitation/create`, `sampling/createMessage`, `roots/list`) over the live session — stamped with the originating request's id for stream association — and re-enters the handler with the collected `inputResponses` until a final result. Handlers are written once in the 2026 `inputRequired(...)` style and serve both eras; the previous loud `-32603` failure remains available via `ServerOptions.inputRequired.legacyShim: false`. Knobs: `inputRequired.maxRounds` (default 8) and `inputRequired.roundTimeoutMs` (default 600 000 ms per leg; legs carry a progressToken so a client reporting progress mid-leg resets the leg timeout). Semantics mirror the modern client driver exactly: per-round replaced `inputResponses`, byte-exact `requestState` echo with the verify hook running every round, paced requestState-only rounds, and elicitation accepted content passed through UNVALIDATED (the handler validates via the schema-aware `acceptedContent` overload, exactly as on the 2026 era). URL-mode legs synthesize the `elicitationId` the 2025-11-25 wire requires. Failures surface per family (`tools/call` → `isError` tool result; `prompts/get` / `resources/read` → JSON-RPC error); stateless legacy HTTP degrades to a clean capability refusal; the shim emits no progress of its own (the originating progressToken is the handler's single must-increase stream — the shim never adds a second author to it).\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:93:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Add `MissingRequiredClientCapabilityError`, the typed error class for the 2026-07-28 `-32021` protocol error (processing a request requires a capability the client did not declare). Its `data.requiredCapabilities` lists the missing capabilities and `ProtocolError.fromError` recognizes the code/data shape. The 2026-07-28 HTTP entry gains a pre-dispatch gate that refuses a request requiring an undeclared client capability with this error and HTTP status `400`; no method served on the 2026-07-28 registry currently carries such a requirement, so observable behavior is unchanged until methods with capability requirements exist.\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:95:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Add the server side of multi round-trip requests (protocol revision 2026-07-28, SEP-2322). Handlers for `tools/call`, `prompts/get`, and `resources/read` can return the value built by `inputRequired()` (exported from the server package together with `acceptedContent()`)\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:101:  wire behavior is unchanged. An optional `ServerOptions.requestState.verify` hook lets a server integrity-check the echoed `requestState` before the handler runs — a throw answers the wire-level `-32602` Invalid Params error with `data.reason: 'invalid_request_state'`; the SDK provides no default verification.\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:110:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - SEP-2243 standard-header server-side validation (protocol revision 2026-07-28). On the modern (2026-07-28) serving path, `createMcpHandler` now enforces the required `Mcp-Method` and `Mcp-Name` standard request headers in addition to the existing `MCP-Protocol-Version` and `Mcp-Method` cross-checks: a modern request without an `Mcp-Method` header, a `tools/call` / `prompts/get` / `resources/read` request without an `Mcp-Name` header, an `Mcp-Name` header carrying an invalid `=?base64?…?=` sentinel, and an `Mcp-Name` header whose (decoded) value disagrees with the body's `params.name` / `params.uri` are all rejected with `400 Bad Request` and JSON-RPC `-32020` (`HeaderMismatch`). The 2025-era serving paths are unchanged.\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:123:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Align the 2026-07-28 protocol error codes to the spec renumber: `HeaderMismatch` is now `-32020` (was `-32001`), `MissingRequiredClientCapability` is now `-32021` (was `-32003`), and `UnsupportedProtocolVersion` is now `-32022` (was `-32004`). These codes are part of the draft 2026-07-28 protocol revision only and have never appeared on a 2025-era wire — the 2025 serving paths and the SDK-conventional `-32001` (`Session not found`) on the stateful Streamable HTTP transport are unchanged. `ProtocolErrorCode.MissingRequiredClientCapability`, `ProtocolErrorCode.UnsupportedProtocolVersion`, the `HEADER_MISMATCH_ERROR_CODE` constant, and the `HEADER_MISMATCH` / `MISSING_REQUIRED_CLIENT_CAPABILITY` / `UNSUPPORTED_PROTOCOL_VERSION` spec-type constants now carry the renumbered values; the `UnsupportedProtocolVersionError` and `MissingRequiredClientCapabilityError` classes (and `ProtocolError.fromError` recognition) follow. The client probe classifier recognizes `-32022` for the corrective continuation and the SEP-2243 one-refresh-on-miss retry triggers on `-32020`.\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:296:    **Tools:** Unknown or disabled tool calls now return JSON-RPC protocol errors with code `-32602` (InvalidParams) instead of `CallToolResult` with `isError: true`. Callers who checked `result.isError` for unknown tools should catch rejected promises instead.\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:298:    **Resources:** Unknown resource reads now return error code `-32002` (ResourceNotFound) instead of `-32602` (InvalidParams).\n./packages/server/CHANGELOG.md:300:    Added `ProtocolErrorCode.ResourceNotFound`.\n./packages/client/test/client/clientTypeSurface.test.ts:27:        expectTypeOf<Awaited<ReturnType<Client['readResource']>>>().toEqualTypeOf<ReadResourceResult>();\n./packages/client/test/client/errorBrandConformance.test.ts:34:        expect(classes.map(([n]) => n)).toContain('ProtocolError');\n./packages/client/test/client/errorBrandConformance.test.ts:63:        'ProtocolError',\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:706: * Parameters for a `resources/read` request.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:708: * @category `resources/read`\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:714: * Sent from the client to the server, to read a specific resource URI.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:716: * @category `resources/read`\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:719:    method: 'resources/read';\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:724: * The server's response to a resources/read request from the client.\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:726: * @category `resources/read`\n./packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2025-11-25.ts:852:     * A URI template (according to RFC 6570) that can be used to construct resource URIs.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:39:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Results of the cacheable 2026-07-28 operations (`tools/list`, `prompts/list`, `resources/list`, `resources/templates/list`, `resources/read`, `server/discover`) now always carry the revision's required `ttlMs`/`cacheScope` fields when served on that revision, defaulting to `ttlMs: 0` / `cacheScope: 'private'`. Servers can configure the emitted values with the new `ServerOptions.cacheHints` option (per operation) and the new `cacheHint` member of the `registerResource` config (per resource); resolution is per field, most specific author first: cache fields returned by a handler win over the per-resource hint, which wins over the per-operation hint, and configured hints are validated at construction/registration time (`RangeError` on invalid values). Responses on 2025-era connections are unchanged and never carry these fields. Note for untyped callers: `registerResource` now interprets a `cacheHint` key in its config object — it is validated and kept out of the resource's list metadata, where it was previously passed through as ordinary metadata.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:52:- [#2381](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2381) [`f0bf785`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/f0bf785239af67f0cfce24575fec9c1193deaff1) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Serve `input_required` handlers on 2025-era connections: the legacy shim (on by default) converts each embedded request of an `input_required` return into a real server→client request (`elicitation/create`, `sampling/createMessage`, `roots/list`) over the live session — stamped with the originating request's id for stream association — and re-enters the handler with the collected `inputResponses` until a final result. Handlers are written once in the 2026 `inputRequired(...)` style and serve both eras; the previous loud `-32603` failure remains available via `ServerOptions.inputRequired.legacyShim: false`. Knobs: `inputRequired.maxRounds` (default 8) and `inputRequired.roundTimeoutMs` (default 600 000 ms per leg; legs carry a progressToken so a client reporting progress mid-leg resets the leg timeout). Semantics mirror the modern client driver exactly: per-round replaced `inputResponses`, byte-exact `requestState` echo with the verify hook running every round, paced requestState-only rounds, and elicitation accepted content passed through UNVALIDATED (the handler validates via the schema-aware `acceptedContent` overload, exactly as on the 2026 era). URL-mode legs synthesize the `elicitationId` the 2025-11-25 wire requires. Failures surface per family (`tools/call` → `isError` tool result; `prompts/get` / `resources/read` → JSON-RPC error); stateless legacy HTTP degrades to a clean capability refusal; the shim emits no progress of its own (the originating progressToken is the handler's single must-increase stream — the shim never adds a second author to it).\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:58:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Add `MissingRequiredClientCapabilityError`, the typed error class for the 2026-07-28 `-32021` protocol error (processing a request requires a capability the client did not declare). Its `data.requiredCapabilities` lists the missing capabilities and `ProtocolError.fromError` recognizes the code/data shape. The 2026-07-28 HTTP entry gains a pre-dispatch gate that refuses a request requiring an undeclared client capability with this error and HTTP status `400`; no method served on the 2026-07-28 registry currently carries such a requirement, so observable behavior is unchanged until methods with capability requirements exist.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:62:  client, an `input_required` answer to `tools/call`, `prompts/get`, or `resources/read` on a 2026-07-28 connection is now fulfilled automatically by default: the embedded requests are dispatched to the client's already-registered elicitation/sampling/roots handlers, and the\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:68:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Add the server side of multi round-trip requests (protocol revision 2026-07-28, SEP-2322). Handlers for `tools/call`, `prompts/get`, and `resources/read` can return the value built by `inputRequired()` (exported from the server package together with `acceptedContent()`)\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:74:  wire behavior is unchanged. An optional `ServerOptions.requestState.verify` hook lets a server integrity-check the echoed `requestState` before the handler runs — a throw answers the wire-level `-32602` Invalid Params error with `data.reason: 'invalid_request_state'`; the SDK provides no default verification.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:76:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - `resources/read` for an unknown URI now answers with JSON-RPC error code `-32602`\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:77:  (Invalid Params) on every protocol revision, with `error.data.uri` echoing the\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:87:    `ProtocolErrorCode.ResourceNotFound` (`-32002`) remains importable as receive-tolerated\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:90:    class carries `data.uri`, and `ProtocolError.fromError` reconstructs it from a `-32602`\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:93:    stays a generic `ProtocolError`.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:99:    The Streamable HTTP transport now emits the `Mcp-Name` standard header on every modern-enveloped request (`params.name` for `tools/call`/`prompts/get`, `params.uri` for `resources/read`), sentinel-encoded.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:101:    **Behavior change (modern era only):** on a modern-enveloped request the Streamable HTTP transport now surfaces an HTTP `400` whose body is a well-formed JSON-RPC error response addressed to the pending request id in-band as a `ProtocolError` (instead of `SdkHttpError`), so the `HEADER_MISMATCH` recovery retry can fire. Legacy-era exchanges are unchanged.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:103:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - SEP-2243 standard-header server-side validation (protocol revision 2026-07-28). On the modern (2026-07-28) serving path, `createMcpHandler` now enforces the required `Mcp-Method` and `Mcp-Name` standard request headers in addition to the existing `MCP-Protocol-Version` and `Mcp-Method` cross-checks: a modern request without an `Mcp-Method` header, a `tools/call` / `prompts/get` / `resources/read` request without an `Mcp-Name` header, an `Mcp-Name` header carrying an invalid `=?base64?…?=` sentinel, and an `Mcp-Name` header whose (decoded) value disagrees with the body's `params.name` / `params.uri` are all rejected with `400 Bad Request` and JSON-RPC `-32020` (`HeaderMismatch`). The 2025-era serving paths are unchanged.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:108:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Align the 2026-07-28 protocol error codes to the spec renumber: `HeaderMismatch` is now `-32020` (was `-32001`), `MissingRequiredClientCapability` is now `-32021` (was `-32003`), and `UnsupportedProtocolVersion` is now `-32022` (was `-32004`). These codes are part of the draft 2026-07-28 protocol revision only and have never appeared on a 2025-era wire — the 2025 serving paths and the SDK-conventional `-32001` (`Session not found`) on the stateful Streamable HTTP transport are unchanged. `ProtocolErrorCode.MissingRequiredClientCapability`, `ProtocolErrorCode.UnsupportedProtocolVersion`, the `HEADER_MISMATCH_ERROR_CODE` constant, and the `HEADER_MISMATCH` / `MISSING_REQUIRED_CLIENT_CAPABILITY` / `UNSUPPORTED_PROTOCOL_VERSION` spec-type constants now carry the renumbered values; the `UnsupportedProtocolVersionError` and `MissingRequiredClientCapabilityError` classes (and `ProtocolError.fromError` recognition) follow. The client probe classifier recognizes `-32022` for the corrective continuation and the SEP-2243 one-refresh-on-miss retry triggers on `-32020`.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:241:    **Tools:** Unknown or disabled tool calls now return JSON-RPC protocol errors with code `-32602` (InvalidParams) instead of `CallToolResult` with `isError: true`. Callers who checked `result.isError` for unknown tools should catch rejected promises instead.\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:243:    **Resources:** Unknown resource reads now return error code `-32002` (ResourceNotFound) instead of `-32602` (InvalidParams).\n./packages/core-internal/CHANGELOG.md:245:    Added `ProtocolErrorCode.ResourceNotFound`.\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:5:import { ProtocolErrorCode } from '../../src/types/enums';\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:8:    ProtocolError,\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:32:        const proto = new ProtocolError(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams, 'bad');\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:33:        expect(proto instanceof ProtocolError).toBe(true);\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:37:        expect(rnf instanceof ProtocolError).toBe(true);\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:45:        const proto = new ProtocolError(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams, 'x');\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:46:        expect(sdk instanceof ProtocolError).toBe(false);\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:61:        expect(protocolErrors.ProtocolError).not.toBe(ProtocolError);\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:66:        expect(foreignHttp instanceof ProtocolError).toBe(false);\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:74:        expect(foreignRnf instanceof ProtocolError).toBe(true);\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:77:        const foreignPlainProto = new protocolErrors.ProtocolError(ProtocolErrorCode.InvalidParams, 'x');\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:78:        expect(foreignPlainProto instanceof ProtocolError).toBe(true);\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:86:    it('ProtocolError.fromError from a second copy reconstructs instances this copy recognizes', async () => {\n./packages/core-internal/test/errors/crossBundleBrand.test.ts:88:    